        "answer": {
          "short": "Swapping the two groups gives the same split, so Jimmy counts every split twice.",
          "worked": "The groups are indistinguishable: “Group 1” and “Group 2” are only labels in Jimmy’s list. Rows 1 and 4 describe the same split, as do rows 2 and 5, and rows 3 and 6. Each split is counted twice, so the actual number is $6\\div2=3$.",
